Upstream bug: https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-147788 (unresolved as of 2026-07)
Subject: [PATCH] a11y: survive table teardown during model changes (macOS crash)

QAccessibleTable::modelChange (fired e.g. by QAbstractItemViewPrivate::
layoutChanged, reached from endMoveRows/rowsMoved) deletes the table's
cached cell interfaces. Each QAccessibleCache::deleteInterface() sends an
ObjectDestroyed event to the platform layer; QCocoaAccessibility::
notifyAccessibilityUpdate resolved it via elementWithId:, which CREATES a
Cocoa element for the cell being deleted if none is cached. That creation
walks the cell's stale row/column indices (possibly -1, from an
invalidated QPersistentModelIndex) and repopulates the table element's
representation — re-entering the caches that are being torn down.

Two crash signatures observed in production (Rebelle 8, Qt 6.11.1,
QTreeView layers panel, with an AX client attached — VoiceOver or any
AX API consumer — while rows are added/moved rapidly):

 1) NSRangeException -> abort():
      -[__NSArrayM objectAtIndexedSubscript:]
      -[QMacAccessibilityElement initWithId:role:]
      +[QMacAccessibilityElement elementWithId:]
      QCocoaAccessibility::notifyAccessibilityUpdate(QAccessibleEvent*)
      QAccessibleCache::deleteInterface(unsigned int, QObject*)
      QAccessibleTable::modelChange(QAccessibleTableModelChangeEvent*)
      QAbstractItemViewPrivate::layoutChanged()
    (guards in initWithId are Q_ASSERTs, compiled out in release builds)

 2) EXC_BAD_ACCESS (KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS, garbage pointer) at
      QAccessibleCache::deleteInterface + 604
      QAccessibleTable::modelChange + 1036
    — container corruption from the re-entrant inserts into the
    hashes being iterated during teardown.

Fix, defense in depth:
 a) qcocoaaccessibility.mm: do not resolve (create) an element for
    ObjectDestroyed events — no case handles them, so creation was the
    event's only, harmful, effect. This removes the re-entrancy at its
    root. Cocoa cleanup of existing elements still happens via
    QAccessibleCache::removeAccessibleElement().
 b) qcocoaaccessibilityelement.mm: turn the debug-only assumptions in
    initWithId:role: into runtime guards — null/validity-check the table
    ancestor, and skip attaching a cell whose stale row/column index is
    negative or out of bounds, instead of indexing past the NSArray.
 c) itemviews.cpp: in the ModelReset branch of modelChange, iterate a
    detached copy of childToId and clear the member first, so re-entrant
    lookups cannot corrupt the iteration. Behavior-neutral otherwise.
---
Addendum (v4): root cause of tables/trees VANISHING from the accessibility
tree after model changes. QMacAccessibilityElement's dealloc (and
removeElementsFromCache) delete the cached interface by the element's axid
— but synthesized placeholder rows/columns/cells share the axid OF THE
TABLE that owns them. updateTableModel replaces the rows/columns arrays on
every table model change; releasing the old placeholder elements therefore
deleted the TABLE's own interface and cached element each time. Confirmed
with qt.accessibility.cache debug logs: the Tree interface of the same
view is deleted and re-registered with a fresh id on every row
insert/remove; the view permanently disappears for assistive clients when
the final dealloc lands after the last re-registration (observed: layers
QTreeView gone for 30+ s after a row delete, revived only by a row
insert). Fix: synthesized placeholders never delete the interface for
their (shared) axid — neither in dealloc nor in removeElementsFromCache.
Realized cells own their axid and are cleaned up as before.
---
Addendum (v5): v4's fix exposed a latent inconsistency that crashed
QAccessibleTable::modelChange near-deterministically (EXC_BAD_ACCESS, 9/10
runs, via QAbstractItemViewPrivate::rowsRemoved). With the table interface
finally persisting (v4), its childToId map accumulates cell ids — but the
platform layer still deletes realized cell interfaces when it releases
their elements, WITHOUT updating childToId. modelChange then dereferences
accessibleInterface(id) == nullptr for a stale id (the Q_ASSERT is
compiled out in release builds). Fix: null-guard stale entries — skip them
in both modelChange iteration branches, and heal-on-access in the child()
lookups (Table/Tree/List variants) by dropping the stale entry and falling
through to create a fresh interface.
